### Page 9 of 14

```text
Saddle Ridge, 13th Filing Annexation
UDC-18-00074

P a g e | 7
PLANCHEYENNE - The application is in accordance with the development policies and physical patterns
identified in the Comprehensive Plan.
This annexation is consistent with PlanCheyenne. The
subject property is within the Urban Service Boundary
(USB) and, per Policy 1.2.B, is encouraged to develop
with an urban character. Policy 1.2.A explains that the
USB is meant to guide urban growth and distinguish
between urban and rural places.
On the future land use map found in PlanCheyenne, the
subject land has been mostly designated as Urban
Residential. The Urban Residential land use designation
includes residential uses as a primary use and includes a
wide variety of supporting and complementary uses as
secondary uses. The applicant is proposing to develop this
property with residential uses, which is identified by
PlanCheyenne as the preferred future land use. The
applicant is also seeking to place a school within the
southern portion of this annexation. Schools are identified
as a preferred secondary use of the Urban Residential
designation.
A portion of the subject property to the north has a future land use designation of Public and Quasi-public.
However, this designation was assigned due to previous ownership of the property by Cheyenne Hills
Church. The property is now owned by the applicant and is adjacent to other Urban Residential uses. The
categories of the Future Land Use map do not wholly pre-determine zones or the uses within those zones.
Map #3 – Future Land Use
Source: Cheyenne/Laramie County GIS
Cooperative Program
